# Daedalus configuration
#
# Copy to .env (./daedalus.sh setup does this for you) and edit as needed.
# .env is gitignored; this file is the tracked template.
#
# Both docker compose and ./daedalus.sh read .env, so one edit here reaches
# the container stack and the local dev servers alike.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ports
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The dashboard and API (one container serves both).
DAEDALUS_PORT=8000

# ChromaDB, exposed on the host so the offline ingestion pipeline can reach it.
CHROMA_PORT=8001

# Used only by `./daedalus.sh dev` (hot reload, no Docker).
BACKEND_PORT=8000
FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The four databases
#
# They are separate on purpose. The sensor database is opened read-only by the
# driver itself, so a bug in ingestion or logging physically cannot reach the
# telemetry of record. See docs/PROJECT.md §6.3.
#
# Paths below are as seen *inside the container*. The host directories that
# back them are set by the volume mounts in docker-compose.yml:
#     ./data          -> /data       (sensor DB, documents, embedded chroma)
#     ./logs          -> /logs       (audit logs)
#     ./backend/data  -> /app/data   (UI preferences)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. SENSOR TELEMETRY — SQLite, READ-ONLY to the AI layer.
#    Written by the SCADA ingestion subsystem. To point Daedalus at a real
#    reactor database, change the `./data` mount in docker-compose.yml to the
#    directory holding it; it is opened read-only regardless.
DAEDALUS_DATA_DIR=/data
#    Resolves to $DAEDALUS_DATA_DIR/sqlite/sensor_readings.db

# 2. AUDIT & EVALUATION LOGS — SQLite, read/write.
#    Chat, tool-call, retrieval, model, error, feedback and memory logs.
DAEDALUS_LOG_DIR=/logs
#    Resolves to $DAEDALUS_LOG_DIR/ai_logs.db

# 3. KNOWLEDGE VECTOR STORE — ChromaDB, read/write.
#    Set: talk to the chromadb service over HTTP (how the stack runs).
#    Unset: fall back to an embedded client writing to $DAEDALUS_DATA_DIR/chroma
#           — that mode needs the full `chromadb` package, not chromadb-client.
CHROMA_URL=http://chromadb:8000

# 4. UI PREFERENCES — SQLite, read/write.
#    Theme and interface state. Deliberately server-side: nothing is kept in
#    browser storage.
DAEDALUS_PREFS_DB=/app/data/prefs.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local model runtime
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Ollama defaults to the host: GPU passthrough is far simpler there and the
# model cache survives container rebuilds.
#   Host (default):        http://host.docker.internal:11434
#   Containerised:         http://ollama:11434
#                          (start it with `./daedalus.sh start --with-ollama`)
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Notes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# There are no secrets here, and that is deliberate: Daedalus runs fully local
# with no cloud APIs in the runtime. If that ever changes, put credentials in
# .env (never .env.example) and keep .env gitignored.
